  "label": "the overallintent",
  "description": "meme-id: camel_meme; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme uses a visual of three camels with their mouths open, juxtaposed with text that mocks Islamic dietary laws by suggesting a contradiction: while pork is considered unclean, camel urine is promoted as 'medicine' based on a reference to Muhammad. This is a deliberately misleading and inflammatory comparison intended to provoke controversy and ridicule. The meme relies on a false equivalence and misrepresentation of religious practices to create a negative impression of Islam. It falls under 'harmful' because it promotes misinformation, stigmatizes a religious group, and can incite prejudice or hostility toward Muslims by distorting their beliefs and practices. The use of the camel image is not merely decorative but serves as a visual pun to reinforce the absurdity of the claim, making the meme more provocative and potentially offensive to its target audience.",
